{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Dynamic Programming \u2014 Policy Iteration & Value Iteration Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: build the GridWorld MDP model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Use the same 4\u00d74 GridWorld from Lesson 01. We add a stochastic variant: with probability `0.1` the agent slips to a random perpendicular direction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "SLIP = 0.1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def transitions(state, action):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if state == TERMINAL:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [(state, 0.0, 1.0)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    outcomes = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for direction, prob in action_probs(action):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        outcomes.append((apply_move(state, direction), -1.0, prob))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return outcomes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`transitions(s, a)` returns a list of `(s', r, p)`. This is the entire model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: policy evaluation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Given a policy `\u03c0(s) = {action: prob}`, iterate the Bellman equation until `V` stops moving:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def policy_evaluation(policy, gamma=0.99, tol=1e-6):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    V = {s: 0.0 for s in states()}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while True:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        delta = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for s in states():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            v = sum(pi_a * sum(p * (r + gamma * V[s_prime])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                              for s_prime, r, p in transitions(s, a))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                   for a, pi_a in policy(s).items())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            delta = max(delta, abs(v - V[s]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            V[s] = v"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if delta < tol:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return V"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: policy improvement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Replace `\u03c0` with the greedy policy w.r.t. `V`. If `\u03c0` did not change, return \u2014 we are at the optimum."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def policy_improvement(V, gamma=0.99):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    new_policy = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for s in states():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        best_a = max("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ACTIONS,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            key=lambda a: sum(p * (r + gamma * V[s_prime])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                              for s_prime, r, p in transitions(s, a)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        new_policy[s] = best_a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return new_policy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: stitch them together"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def policy_iteration(gamma=0.99):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    policy = {s: \"up\" for s in states()}   # arbitrary start"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(100):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        V = policy_evaluation(lambda s: {policy[s]: 1.0}, gamma)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        new_policy = policy_improvement(V, gamma)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if new_policy == policy:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return V, policy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        policy = new_policy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Typical convergence on 4\u00d74: 4\u20136 outer iterations. Outputs `V*(0,0) \u2248 -6` and a policy that strictly decreases the step count."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: value iteration (the one-loop version)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def value_iteration(gamma=0.99, tol=1e-6):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    V = {s: 0.0 for s in states()}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while True:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        delta = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for s in states():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            v = max(sum(p * (r + gamma * V[s_prime])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                       for s_prime, r, p in transitions(s, a))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                   for a in ACTIONS)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            delta = max(delta, abs(v - V[s]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            V[s] = v"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if delta < tol:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    policy = policy_improvement(V, gamma)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return V, policy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Same fixed point, fewer lines of code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run value iteration on the 4\u00d74 GridWorld with `\u03b3 \u2208 {0.9, 0.99}`. How many sweeps until `max |\u0394V| < 1e-6`? Print `V*` as a 4\u00d74 grid.\n2. **Medium.** Compare policy iteration vs value iteration on the *stochastic* GridWorld (slip probability `0.1`). Count: sweeps, wall-clock time, final `V*(0,0)`. Which converges faster in iterations? In wall-clock?\n3. **Hard.** Build modified policy iteration: in the evaluation step, run only `k` sweeps instead of to convergence. Plot `V*(0,0)` error vs `k` for `k \u2208 {1, 2, 5, 10, 50}`. What does the curve tell you about the evaluation/improvement tradeoff?"
      ]
    }
